// Chunk 51, finding gap-g9#1 (its trace verifier's test). The phrase is open in two Chrome profiles, as privacy.md's
// "A separate Chrome profile keeps cookies apart" suggests for sites. Profile A (this one) made 500 ₳ (U) and 60 ₳
// (O) private from public account 0. Profile B, with no history of A's, funds a private session from U: its funding
// F_B pays the one-time account and returns its change C (394.6 ₳) to the contract under a fresh register. On B, C is
// that session's money. On A, the next reading finds U gone and C new; F_B isn't in A's sealed history, so `arrived`
// notes C as a payment received (activity.ts:441-450, no origin past the first reading) and `classes` gives it
// received:<F_B> (activity.ts:656-657), origin "received" ("Paid by someone else", build.rs Origin::Received). Activity
// titles it Received (and Save as CSV exports it so), the UTxOs screen tags it Received, and a new session's funding
// on A, Purpose::Fund, ranks it 1 ahead of A's own O at 4 (build.rs:2401-2411; one_more, smallest of the best rank
// first, build.rs:2603-2628): it spends C, tying the new session to B's on chain, and its review has no note
// (spentHistories gives one class, historiesNote says nothing for one). One device holding both, whose history has
// F_B as its own session's funding, classes C as that session's money (rank 5) and takes O: privacy.md's Co-spending
// says "a session's funding takes ... another session's money last". The control below shows that. This asserts the
// right behaviour, so it fails while the bug is there.
import { describe, expect, it } from "vitest";

import { txInputs } from "../src/background/cbor";
import { registerOf } from "../src/background/chain";
import type { KoiosUtxo } from "../src/background/koios";
import { SESSION_OUT } from "../src/background/sessions";
import { historiesNote, historyTags, madePrivate, merged, sessionClass } from "../src/shared/histories";
import type { PendingTx } from "../src/shared/rpc";
import { activityTitle } from "../src/ui/activity";
import { busyFor, minswapEstimate, ownedUtxos, testBalances, vectors, withdrawPreprod } from "./fakes";

const PASSWORD = "correct horse battery";
const PHRASE = vectors("cardano_account.json").find((v) => v.account === 0 && v.phrase.split(" ").length === 12)!.phrase as string;
const hexOf = (b: Uint8Array) => Buffer.from(b).toString("hex");
const [M1, M2, FB] = ["a5", "a6", "fb"].map((h) => h.repeat(32)) as [string, string, string];
/** The other profile's session, as its own book numbers it. */
const B_SESSION = 7;

/**
 * Profile A's view after the other profile's funding F_B: U (M1#0) spent by it, its change C (FB#2) new, O (M2#0)
 * untouched; then a private swap's funding built here. `sentHere`: F_B is in this profile's history, as on one device.
 */
async function profileA(sentHere: boolean) {
  const t = testBalances({ owned: false });
  await t.wallet.create(PHRASE, PASSWORD);
  const { wasm } = t.deps;
  // Every output of the wallet goes under a fresh re-randomization of its register, in either profile.
  const base = registerOf(ownedUtxos[0]!)!;
  const fresh = () => hexOf(wasm.registerToDatum(wasm.rerandomize(new wasm.Register(base.generator, base.publicValue))));
  const row = (txHash: string, txIndex: number, lovelace: string, height: number, time: number): KoiosUtxo => ({
    ...ownedUtxos[0]!,
    tx_hash: txHash,
    tx_index: txIndex,
    value: lovelace,
    asset_list: [],
    inline_datum: { bytes: fresh(), value: null },
    block_height: height,
    block_time: time,
  });
  const sent = (kind: PendingTx["kind"], txHash: string): PendingTx => ({ kind, network: "preprod", txHash, submittedAt: t.clock.now, confirmations: null });

  // 500 ₳ and 60 ₳ made private from public account 0: this profile's history has both move-ins.
  await t.activity.sent("preprod", sent("move-in", M1), { lovelace: "500000000", origin: madePrivate(0) });
  await t.activity.sent("preprod", sent("move-in", M2), { lovelace: "60000000", origin: madePrivate(0) });
  const began = Math.floor(t.clock.now / 1000);
  const U = row(M1, 0, "500000000", 9_000_001, began + 20);
  const O = row(M2, 0, "60000000", 9_000_002, began + 40);
  t.koios.added.push(U, O);
  await t.balances.get("preprod");
  const own = await t.activity.classes("preprod", [U, O]);
  expect([...own.values()]).toEqual([madePrivate(0), madePrivate(0)]);

  // F_B funds a site's private session from U and returns its change C to the contract. One device that sent it
  // wrote it down as that session's funding (sessions.ts buildFunding's summary: its change carries U's history).
  if (sentHere) {
    await t.activity.sent("preprod", sent("session-out", FB), {
      index: B_SESSION,
      lovelace: "105000000",
      origin: merged([madePrivate(0), sessionClass(B_SESSION)]),
    });
  }
  // The next reading, a full one (a Koios catch-up shows a spend made elsewhere only at the next full read): U is
  // gone and C is new.
  t.koios.spent.add(`${M1}#0`);
  const C = row(FB, 2, "394600000", 9_000_010, began + 900);
  t.koios.added.push(C);
  await busyFor(t, 31 * 60_000);
  await t.balances.get("preprod", true);
  const { seedelf: rows } = await t.coins.lists("preprod");
  expect(rows.some((u) => u.txHash === M1)).toBe(false);
  expect(rows.some((u) => u.txHash === M2 && u.index === 0)).toBe(true);
  const cRow = rows.find((u) => u.txHash === FB && u.index === 2);
  expect(cRow).toBeDefined();
  const entry = (await t.activity.seedelf("preprod")).find((e) => e.txHash === FB);
  const cClass = (await t.activity.classes("preprod", [O, C])).get(`${FB}#2`);

  // A private swap here: a new session's funding (Purpose::Fund), which one UTxO pays alone.
  const evaluation = withdrawPreprod.amount.evaluation as { result: unknown[] };
  t.koios.evaluation = { ...evaluation, result: evaluation.result.slice(0, 1) };
  const quote = await t.sessions.quote("preprod", minswapEstimate.ask);
  const out = await t.sessions.outBuild("preprod", quote);
  const kept = (await t.session.get<{ txCbor: string }>(SESSION_OUT))!;
  const inputs = txInputs(Uint8Array.from(Buffer.from(kept.txCbor, "hex")));
  // As the swap's review shows it (Swaps.tsx HistoriesNote).
  const note = historiesNote(out.histories, { session: out.index });
  const label = sentHere ? "one device" : "profile A";
  console.log(
    `[r51 gap-g9#1] ${label}: F_B in Activity ${JSON.stringify(entry && { kind: entry.kind, title: activityTitle(entry), lovelace: entry.lovelace })}; ` +
      `C classed ${JSON.stringify(cClass)}, tagged ${JSON.stringify(cRow?.history && historyTags(cRow.history))}`,
  );
  console.log(`[r51 gap-g9#1] ${label}: session ${out.index}'s funding spends ${JSON.stringify(inputs)}; histories ${JSON.stringify(out.histories)}, note ${JSON.stringify(note)}`);
  return { entry, cClass, cRow, inputs, note };
}

describe("the phrase open in a second profile (chunk 51, gap-g9#1)", () => {
  it("never reads that profile's own session change as a payment received, nor funds a new session from it silently", { timeout: 180_000 }, async () => {
    // The control: one device holding the same UTxOs, which sent F_B itself, funds the new session from O.
    const oneDevice = await profileA(true);
    expect(oneDevice.cClass).toEqual({ id: `public:0+session:${B_SESSION}`, origin: "session" });
    expect(oneDevice.inputs).toEqual([`${M2}#0`]);

    const here = await profileA(false);
    // C is no one else's payment: the phrase's own change, sent from the other profile.
    expect.soft(here.entry && activityTitle(here.entry), "Activity doesn't call the other profile's change a payment received").not.toBe("Received");
    expect.soft(here.cClass?.origin, "C isn't classed as money someone else paid").not.toBe("received");
    expect.soft(here.cRow?.history && historyTags(here.cRow.history), "the UTxOs screen doesn't tag it Received").not.toContain("Received");
    // So the funding doesn't silently tie this session to the other profile's: it takes the money made private here,
    // as the one device does, or its review says what spending C ties.
    const tiesSilently = here.inputs.includes(`${FB}#2`) && here.note === undefined;
    expect.soft(tiesSilently, "the funding doesn't spend the other profile's session change ahead of O with no note").toBe(false);
  });
});

// Chunk 51, gap-g6#1 (the trace verifier's test). On mainnet the private index's sealed record (`contract.mainnet`,
// contract-scan.ts `Settled`) keeps the wallet's verdict on each contract row: `rows`, those judged ours as of the
// stable cursor, never checked again, and `checked`, those above it, each judged once by ref. A row judged not ours
// is never kept: once the cursor passes it, nothing says it was there (contract-scan.ts:281, 294-297, 301, 315-318).
// The record's only version is its format's, `v: 1`, the gate at contract-scan.ts:264, and nothing ties a verdict to
// the rule that made it (chain.ts registerOf, balances.ts ownedUtxos, the WebAssembly's isOwned). An update leaves
// chrome.storage.local as it was (sw.ts's onInstalled only re-applies two preferences), so the next release reads
// 1.9.1's record and serves its verdicts as its own.
//
// Chunk 51's fix round changes that rule in both directions: x2#2's fix refuses a row at a KEY address with the
// contract's hash, which 1.9.1 seals into `rows` as ours; and r3a#1's class, if chain.ts's registerOf learns the
// indefinite pair 102([_ 0, [g, u]]), takes a payment 1.9.1 sealed as not ours. Neither rule is in this tree, so this
// build's own rule plays the new one, and the record is written as 1.9.1 (`v: 1`) seals it under a rule that
// disagreed with it:
// - another wallet's row, which this build refuses, kept in `rows` as ours: x2#2's direction;
// - a payment to this wallet above the cursor, which this build takes, kept as `checked: false`: r3a#1's.
//
// What's right (the finding's fix): a record sealed under another rule is never served, e.g. `Settled.v` bumped in
// the release that changes the rule, so 264 reads one snapshot and this build's rule judges every row. Today the
// first row is counted in the private balance, the second never is, and once the cursor passes the second the
// record keeps no trace of it: only a snapshot (Remove wallet and a restore, a rollback, a refused cursor) finds it.
import type * as Wasm from "@seedelf/wasm";
import { describe, expect, it } from "vitest";

import { CONTRACT_V1, ownedUtxos as ownedByRule } from "../src/background/balances";
import { seedelfTokenOf, sumValue } from "../src/background/chain";
import { readContractView, type ContractView } from "../src/background/contract-scan";
import { DataParts } from "../src/background/data-layer";
import { privateIndexClient, utxoOf, type IndexRow } from "../src/background/private-index";
import { outpoint } from "../src/background/spent";
import { fakeIndex, indexRowOf } from "./fake-index";
import { koiosPreprod, loadTestWasm, ownedUtxos, testBalances, vectors } from "./fakes";

const PASSWORD = "correct horse battery";
const OURS = ownedUtxos.map(outpoint).sort();

/** The record as contract-scan.ts seals it (its `Settled`, not exported). */
interface SealedView {
  v: number;
  owner: string;
  cursor: string;
  got: number;
  rows: IndexRow[];
  checked: Record<string, boolean>;
}

/** What the private balance counts of a view (balances.ts spendableOwned, then sumValue): lovelace. */
const privateLovelace = (view: ContractView) =>
  sumValue(view.owned.filter((u) => !seedelfTokenOf(u, CONTRACT_V1.seedelfPolicyId) && !u.reference_script)).lovelace;

/** The 12-word wallet unlocked on mainnet's private index, as private-index.test.ts's onIndex sets it up. */
async function onIndex() {
  const v = vectors("cardano_account.json").find((v) => v.account === 0 && v.phrase.split(" ").length === 12)!;
  const t = testBalances();
  await t.wallet.create(v.phrase, PASSWORD);
  const index = fakeIndex();
  const base = index.tip - 100_000;
  index.contract = [...koiosPreprod.contract_utxos, ...ownedUtxos].map((u) => ({ row: indexRowOf(u, base) }));
  const parts = new DataParts(t.session, () => t.clock.now);
  const deps = {
    ...t.deps,
    wasm: loadTestWasm() as typeof Wasm,
    index: privateIndexClient(
      { koiosOnly: async () => false, parts, fetch: index.fetch, limits: {} },
      (n) => (n === "mainnet" ? "https://data.test" : undefined),
    ),
  };
  const record = () => t.deps.store.get<SealedView>("contract.mainnet");
  /** Seals the record as 1.9.1 would have, under a rule that judged these rows otherwise than this build does. */
  const sealAs191 = async (change: Partial<SealedView>) => {
    const kept = (await record())!;
    await t.deps.store.set("contract.mainnet", { ...kept, ...change, v: 1 });
  };
  /** This build's verdict on one index row, outside the record. */
  const ruleSays = (row: IndexRow) =>
    t.wallet.withKeys((keys) => ownedByRule(deps.wasm, keys, [utxoOf(row, CONTRACT_V1.walletContractHash)]).length === 1);
  return { t, index, deps, record, sealAs191, ruleSays };
}

describe("r51 gap-g6#1: the sealed contract view's verdicts after the rule that made them changed", { timeout: 120_000 }, () => {
  it("never counts a row the record kept as ours that this build's rule refuses (x2#2's direction)", async () => {
    const { index, deps, record, sealAs191, ruleSays } = await onIndex();
    // A restore: the snapshot, every row judged by this build, sealed. 28 ₳ private (25 + 3; the Seedelf's 1.5 ₳ is
    // listed, not counted).
    const first = await readContractView(deps, "mainnet");
    expect(first.owned.map(outpoint).sort()).toEqual(OURS);
    expect(privateLovelace(first)).toBe(28_000_000n);

    // Another wallet's 4.83 ₳ row with no Seedelf, still unspent at the contract: this build's rule refuses it.
    const theirs = index.contract.map((r) => r.row).find((r) => !OURS.includes(r.ref) && r.datum && !r.assets)!;
    expect(theirs.lovelace).toBe("4828227");
    expect(await ruleSays(theirs)).toBe(false);
    // The record 1.9.1 left, under a rule that took that row.
    await sealAs191({ rows: [...(await record())!.rows, theirs] });

    // The update: this build reads that record.
    const after = await readContractView(deps, "mainnet");
    expect.soft(after.owned.map(outpoint)).not.toContain(theirs.ref);
    expect.soft(privateLovelace(after)).toBe(28_000_000n);
  });

  it("counts a payment the record kept as not ours that this build's rule takes, before and after the cursor passes it (r3a#1's class)", async () => {
    const { index, deps, record, sealAs191, ruleSays } = await onIndex();
    await readContractView(deps, "mainnet");
    // 25 ₳ paid to this wallet's register in the last few blocks: above any stable cursor. This build's rule takes it.
    const paid = { ...indexRowOf(ownedUtxos[0]!, index.tip - 50), ref: `${"b3".repeat(32)}#0` };
    index.contract.push({ row: paid });
    expect(await ruleSays(paid)).toBe(true);
    // 1.9.1 saw it once and judged it not ours, as it judges a payment spelled 102([_ 0, [g, u]]).
    await readContractView(deps, "mainnet");
    await sealAs191({ checked: { [paid.ref]: false } });

    // The update, before the cursor passes it.
    const after = await readContractView(deps, "mainnet");
    expect.soft(after.owned.map(outpoint)).toContain(paid.ref);
    expect.soft(privateLovelace(after)).toBe(53_000_000n);

    // The cursor passes it: it should be settled as ours, as any payment of ours is (private-index.test.ts:87).
    index.advance(400);
    const later = await readContractView(deps, "mainnet");
    expect.soft(later.owned.map(outpoint)).toContain(paid.ref);
    expect.soft((await record())!.rows.map((r) => r.ref)).toContain(paid.ref);
  });
});

trace.reason:
The finding holds as described, and a run shows it. When a pool read asks what made a box, accountKeys checks only the active account, the known accounts and accounts 0-23. lookUp then seals the answer by transaction, and nothing asks again: not found, not made, not lookUp, and no account handler. So suppose a restored wallet reads the pool (when Lovejoin's page opens) before the user adds custom account 30 back. Account 30's deposit is sealed as `{mixed:false}` with no `public`.

After `add(30)`:
- the sealed origin is unchanged;
- the page names no account;
- Mix my boxes again from the private balance counts both boxes (`{boxes: 2, owned: 2}`) and fanOut puts them first;
- a box brought back records no tie (depositAccountOf gives undefined).

The control shows the timing is the only cause: account 30 added before the first read is refused, as account 1 is. I found no guard the finder missed. Production wiring matches the fixture: sw.ts:209 and fakes.ts:722 wire knownAccounts the same way. It is not settled anywhere.

I grade it low, agreeing with the finder. The cost is medium in kind: a privacy link made by default, the same mechanism as e1a#1. But reaching it is an edge case of the user's own setup, with three conditions:
- a custom-numbered account of index 24 or more, reached only by add or check;
- that account's boxes still sitting in a pool at their deposit (a public Bootstrap's held boxes, or a chain cut after its deposit);
- a restore or a second browser where Lovejoin is opened before the account is added back.

No money is at risk. Once sealed, no screen offers a way out. Adding the account before opening Lovejoin avoids it, but nothing says so.

